  <reporting-org ref="XI-IATI-EC_INTPA" secondary-reporter="0" type="15">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">European Commission - Directorate-General for International Partnerships</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sophakama: Building civic agency and strengthening social accountability across rural municipalities as a response to poor governance, weak finance management and lack of service delivery</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Overall objective&lt;/strong&gt;: An active and empowered citizenry emerges across rural South Africa and actively holds local government accountable for basic service delivery thereby improving the state&#xbf;s capacity for service delivery in rural South Africa and good local governance; this would in turn contribute to addressing the devastating socio-economic conditions in rural areas and former homelands.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specific objective&lt;/strong&gt;: Community leadership in rural municipalities are empowered and supported to hold decision-makers in rural municipalities accountable for the decisions they make on service delivery and for how public resources are utilized as a means of advancing their socio-economic rights.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
